sual art</strong></a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n \n\n\n  <p>I think I bought water soluble color pencils in multiple shades of blue that day from <a href=\"https://www.modulor.de/en/\" target=\"_blank\">modulor in berlin</a> <em>(extremely dangerous place!!!)</em> — and, as is the case recently, I felt like a body bag carrying a thousand glass shards, so I painted this during a weekly time magic co-working session I organized for <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">Labyrinth</a>, and ended up writing some words in it, giving form to the screaming questions in my head, to no one in particular. </p><p>I thought about how broken glass resembles water or rivers, but leading nowhere. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/04bef03c-e7b7-4f8d-93da-21202da1102f/glassrivers3.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/04bef03c-e7b7-4f8d-93da-21202da1102f/glassrivers3.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/04bef03c-e7b7-4f8d-93da-21202da1102f/glassrivers3.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/04bef03c-e7b7-4f8d-93da-21202da1102f/glassrivers3.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/04bef03c-e7b7-4f8d-93da-21202da1102f/glassrivers3.jpeg?f